  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1617.07 Precautions",
  "priorExpiration": "2005-01-10",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1617.07 Precautions.\n\n(a) Magazine doors shall be kept locked, except during the time of placement and removal of stocks of explosives or during inspection.\n\n(b) When any explosive is removed from a magazine for use, the oldest stock shall be removed first.\n\n(c) Black powder, when stored in magazines with other explosives, shall be segregated.\n\n(d) No explosive shall be left unattended or unsecured at construction sites or other similar operations.\n\nSource. #2220, eff 12-31-82; ss by #2837, eff 8-27-84; ss by #4584, eff 3-3-89; ss by #5996, INTERIM, eff 3-3-95, EXPIRES, 7-1-95; ss by #6054, eff 7-1-95, EXPIRED: 7-1-03\n\nNew. #8116, INTERIM, eff 7-14-04, EXPIRES: 1-10-05; ss by #8231, eff 12-20-04; ss by #10396, eff 8-15-13",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c1600.html"
